# Modernization patterns

Slap's pre-modernization codebase used Bluebird, prototype-chain inheritance,
and several abandoned slap-editor satellite packages. Those are gone. Don't
reintroduce them.

## Promises: native, not Bluebird

| Bluebird                     | Native equivalent                                   |
| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| `Promise.method(fn)`         | `async function`                                    |
| `.tap(fn)`                   | `.then(v => { fn(v); return v; })` or just `await`  |
| `.return(x)`                 | `.then(() => x)`                                    |
| `.spread(([a,b]) => …)`      | destructuring: `.then(([a, b]) => …)`               |
| `.done()`                    | remove (native rejections auto-throw in modern Node)|
| `.call('method')`            | `.then(v => v.method())`                            |
| `Promise.promisifyAll(fs)`   | `fs.promises` / `require('fs').promises`            |
| `Promise.promisify(fn)`      | `require('util').promisify(fn)`                     |
| `Promise.try(fn)`            | `(async () => fn())()` or just call from async fn   |
| `global.Promise = Bluebird`  | delete                                              |

## ES6 classes, not `__proto__`

Don't write:

```js
function Foo(opts) { Bar.call(this, opts); /* ... */ }
Foo.prototype.__proto__ = Bar.prototype;
Foo.prototype.method = function () { … };
```

Write:

```js
class Foo extends Bar {
  constructor(opts) { super(opts); /* ... */ }
  method() { … }
}
```

For the mixin case (extending a built-in + needing BaseWidget behavior), see
[widget-conventions](widget-conventions.mdc).

## Banned package names

These are abandoned and NOT in our dep tree. If you see one being
suggested/added, that's a regression — use the local replacement instead:

| Don't add        | Use instead                                    |
| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| `bluebird`       | native `Promise`, `async`/`await`              |
| `base-widget`    | `require('./BaseWidget')` (slap) / `require('./BaseWidget')` (fork) |
| `slap-util`      | `require('../slap-util')` (slap) / `require('./util')` (fork) |
| `editor-widget` from npm | the vendored tarball (slap) — already wired |
| `node-clap`      | `lib/plugin-loader.js`                         |
| `mkdirp`         | `fs.promises.mkdir(p, { recursive: true })`    |
| `traverse`       | `lib/util/helpers.js#mapDeep`                  |
| `winston`        | the streaming logger in `lib/slap-util.js`     |

## text-buffer 9 marker properties

`textBuf.markPosition(point, options)` in 9.x **drops** custom properties
like `{type: 'foo'}` (only forwards `tailed` + `invalidate`). Always set
custom marker types via `setProperties` after creation:

```js
var marker = textBuf.markPosition(p, { invalidate: 'never' });
marker.setProperties({ type: 'selection' });
```

`markRange` *does* still accept custom properties (with a deprecation
warning), so existing `markRange(range, { type: 'findMatch' })` callsites
in `FindForm` etc. still work.
